    "lawCode": "Amd §2799-ggg, Pub Auth L; amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8736A\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to authorizing\nthe Syracuse regional airport authority to provide and maintain an\nauthority police department and a uniformed authority police force\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAmends the enabling legislation of the Syracuse Regional Airport Author-\nity to authorize the authority to form its own police force to provide\nsecurity at Hancock International Airport.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Authorizes the Syracuse Regional Airport Authority to estab-\nlish its own police force to provide policing and security at the\nAirport.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Syracuse Regional Airport Authority (\"Authority\") was created by\nstatute in 2011 to improve and modernize the operation of the Hancock\nInternational Airport (\"Hancock\") in Syracuse, NY. To date, the Authori-\nty has successfully managed the operation of the Airport and accom-\nplished its goal of better coordinating air travel in Central New York.\nOver the last decade, the Authority made extensive renovations and\nimprovements to Hancock's terminal and infrastructure and successfully\nattracted new carriers to the Airport.\n\nNow, with a decade of operating experience, the Authority has identified\na series of initiatives that will further improve operations and expand\nservices at Hancock. Most critical, the Authority seeks authorization to\nestablish its own police force.  Currently, officers of the Syracuse\nPolice Department (\"SPD\") patrol the Airport, including the TSA check-\npoints. Due to ongoing staffing issues with SPD, it is becoming more\ndifficult to properly staff the Airport. Allowing the Authority to\nestablish its own police force will allow it to avoid future staffing\nconflicts with SPD. Currently, both the Port Authority of NY and NJ and\nthe Niagara-Frontier Transit Authority have this authorization.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill (Amending Chapter 463 of 2011).\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
